Introduction to Angular:

What is Angular?
  1. It is frontend JavaScript Framework{useful for building interatcive web applications}.
  2. collection of Tools and features{ CLI(using commands to create app,components, modules etc),debugging tools, IDE plugins}
  Note: It is a framework(which helps in providing tools and libraries to build web Applications)

Why to use Angular ?
  1. Popular,
  2. Simplifies the process of building complex interatcive UI's easily
  3. Flexible,
  4. OOPs concepts and principles
  5. uses TypeScript

Why components ?
   1. break up complex applications into simple building blocks.
   2. Build up once and re-use it.
   3. Useful in development process, componentscan be divided and working happens concurrently across teams.
   4. Reduce dependenices.

Angular CLI:

Angular CLI is a command line interface which is used to initialize, develop and maintain Angular Applications 
directly from command shell
** Useful fro
  1. Running development server
  2. deploying the appication   
  3. Testing of Application (npm run test)

For creating component -> ng generate component "component name here" or ng g c "component name here"
       example: ng g c user { It creates html,css, ts file, spec.ts file}
If wanted to skip test cases file i.e spec.ts file
      ng g c component-name --skip-tests=true  (or) 
      ng generate component component-name --skip-tests=true

For creating module -> ng generate module module-name (or) ng g m module-name

For creating service -> ng generate service service-name (or) ng g s service-name

To run Angular application run command
  ng serve (or) ng serve --o {by default it run on  http://localhost:4200/ }

Features:
1. Standalone
2. Uses Signals
